Original commit body from 7f43c94bb9c47cc37a6bc1b94c96693e24e1b473:

Span helpers in router_routes/controller_routes, tree-cursor walkers in
fingerprint, **kwargs: Any in the analyzer registry, RegisteredLinker in
pass_metadata, and the two view-template linkers.

OPTIONAL-DEPENDENCY ANNOTATIONS. view_template_laravel and
view_template_spring import tree-sitter INSIDE A TRY, because these
linkers degrade gracefully when the optional grammar is absent. Their
annotations therefore name Optional["tree_sitter.Parser"] under
TYPE_CHECKING and the runtime import graph is untouched. A module-scope
import added to satisfy an annotation would convert "this linker quietly
does nothing" into "the tool fails to start". Same reasoning for css.py
and toml_config.py in the previous batch.

FOUR MORE UNGUARDED Node.text DEREFERENCES, AND THE FIX DIFFERS PER SITE.
tree_sitter.Node.text is `bytes | None`. Annotating the node parameters
exposed four bare .text.decode(...) calls in view_template_spring:

  * two decode text that is immediately COMPARED (== method_short_name,
    != "ModelAndView"). An empty-string default is correct there — the
    comparison fails and existing logic handles the non-match.
  * two decode text that BECOMES A VIEW NAME emitted as an edge. An
    empty-string default would mint a reference to a view whose name
    could not be read: a silent wrong-value bug, strictly worse than the
    crash it replaces. Those bail (return None / continue).

A blanket `if X.text else ""` across all four would have satisfied mypy,
passed every test, and introduced empty-named edges. Same shape as the
Counter[int]-on-string-keys error earlier in this campaign: the pattern
is uniform, the correct answer is not.

THIS IS NOW A MEASURED CLASS: 34 .text.decode( sites in packages/*/src/,
27 guarded, ~7 not. The unguarded ones are INVISIBLE to mypy until their
receiver is annotated, because an untyped parameter makes node.text an
Any. Two files found so far, each by annotating something else, and each
half-guarding its own idiom. They surface one batch at a time, which the
blocking whole-tree ratchet turns into a forcing function rather than a
leak.

pass_metadata takes RegisteredLinker as a DIRECT runtime import, not a
type-only one: the module already imports get_all_linkers from that same
module, so the cycle a TYPE_CHECKING import would avoid does not exist.

Baseline ratcheted 797 -> 766. 15903 tests pass.

